title: metafit
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mário
    family-names: Antunes
    email: mario.antunes@av.it.pt
    affiliation: Instituto de Telecomunicações, University of Aveiro
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6504-9441'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/mariolpantunes/aiml-model'
abstract: >-
  Interpretable linear meta-models that predict the Matthews Correlation
  Coefficient of a classifier from dataset and model meta-features. Equations
  take the form MCC = w1*t1 + w2*t2 + ..., where each term is a simple
  expression over one to three raw features and each weight is stated in the
  features' own units. Terms are drawn from a filtered candidate library,
  screened by paired Pearson and Spearman correlation, and selected by beam
  search with ridge refitting. Two equations are contrasted: one over dataset
  features alone, which can only predict a per-dataset constant, and one over
  dataset and model features, isolating how much of MCC is attributable to
  model capability. Validation is leave-one-dataset-out and leave-one-model-out;
  the leakage induced by random k-fold splitting on grouped meta-data is
  quantified rather than assumed away.
keywords:
  - meta-learning
  - algorithm-selection
  - symbolic-regression
  - sparse-regression
  - interpretability
  - matthews-correlation-coefficient
  - model-selection
